				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weizhong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1777811); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1777811&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607936109" alt="weizhong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1777811)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weizhong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1777811); return false;" >weizhong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1391301826 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Feb 2014 00:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1954055">
									

<p>Thanks to Voct, CryogenChaos, Djoric, TwistedGears, Iceforge, Wogglebug, and many, many other chat users who read through this and helped craft this skip into what it is now.</p>
<p>The inspiration for this came from the idea of damnatio memoriae: I was reading about the Turin King List (aka a list of Egyptian pharaohs), and a few entries were wiped out, or too damaged to read. My imagination went &quot;Hey, what if that was intentional,&quot; and this happened.</p>
<p>EDIT: Oh, and the image is from the Global Egyptian Museum.</p>

