			<div class="content" id="post-content-1954605">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Threats of violence, up to, and including death as a punishment for refusing to enter SCP-1644's active area have failed, as individuals will continue to refuse to enter SCP-1644, even when such threats have been carried out.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is unintentionally hilarious. &quot;If you don't go into the area, I will kill you.&quot; &quot;No! I&#8230; I can't.&quot; *BANG* &quot;Still won't go in?&quot; &#8230; &quot;All right, mark that down, he's continuing to refuse.&quot;</p>
<p>This doesn't really improve it too much either. Now we've got some mythical book that allegedly contains an immortality ritual. I still don't see how this warrants the AMNESTICS-ARE-CANDY containment, and the general over-the-topness of this. Cripes, we've got so many immortality methods already, and in real life, there's so many legends of rulers who sought immortality. What makes this special?</p>

